WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.627 --> 00:00:03.727
Could aliens destroy us
from light years away?

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:07.427
Mh, another day at the Kurzgesagt Labs,

00:00:07.494 --> 00:00:10.794
where we answer the most important
questions with science.

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:11.894
Today:

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:15.360
how might civilizations wage war
across light years?

00:00:15.427 --> 00:00:18.127
What kind of devastating weapons
could they use,

00:00:18.194 --> 00:00:19.894
and what would they look like?

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:21.660
Meet our two players.

00:00:21.727 --> 00:00:25.394
A yellow dwarf star system
home to a species of primates.

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:27.360
"Humans," as they call themselves,

00:00:27.427 --> 00:00:30.160
recently became
a technological civilization.

00:00:30.227 --> 00:00:33.694
They have rockets,
nuclear reactors and memes.

00:00:33.794 --> 00:00:34.994
How cute!

00:00:35.694 --> 00:00:37.827
The Smorpians disagree.

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:43.227
They reside on a planet around
the orange dwarf star HD 40307,

00:00:43.294 --> 00:00:44.760
42 light years away.

00:00:45.094 --> 00:00:48.094
Smorpian civilization
developed earlier than humans

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:50.360
and they have much better technology.

00:00:50.627 --> 00:00:53.160
They've recently built
a Dyson swarm around their star

00:00:53.227 --> 00:00:55.260
which gives them near limitless energy.

00:00:55.327 --> 00:00:57.494
And they noticed humanity,

00:00:57.560 --> 00:01:00.960
which is unfortunate as the Smorpians
are planning a hyperspace bypass

00:01:01.027 --> 00:01:02.427
through our solar system,

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:05.360
so they decided that humanity has to go.

00:01:05.594 --> 00:01:07.994
Interstellar war is hard though.

00:01:08.294 --> 00:01:12.294
Front lines, tactics, and logistics
are meaningless at these scales.

00:01:12.797 --> 00:01:14.637
It's also fought across time.

00:01:15.027 --> 00:01:17.260
Decades will pass
between firing a weapon

00:01:17.327 --> 00:01:19.194
and learning whether it hit or not.

00:01:19.727 --> 00:01:22.294
Sending an invasion fleet is futile.

00:01:22.694 --> 00:01:26.027
Even if the Smorpians travel
in a large fraction of the speed of light,

00:01:26.094 --> 00:01:29.294
the journey to Earth would take
decades or even centuries,

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:32.560
and humans would have
plenty of time to prepare.

00:01:32.727 --> 00:01:35.194
If you want to learn more
about the mind numbing problem

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:37.260
of war between alien civilizations,

00:01:37.327 --> 00:01:39.027
we made a video about it.

00:01:39.327 --> 00:01:42.194
Today we'll help the Smorpians
construct a weapon

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:46.294
that is not only extremely long range
and as fast as physically possible,

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:48.860
but that will totally destroy
everything on Earth,

00:01:48.927 --> 00:01:53.227
so no human survivors will come to an act
of vengeance on swap in the future.

00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:57.127
In interstellar war,
you want to win with one shot.

00:01:57.527 --> 00:02:01.127
Our bird scientists have found
three Smorpian designs:

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:04.194
the Star Laser, the Relativistic Missile,

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:06.860
and the Ultra-Relativistic Electron Beam.

00:02:07.427 --> 00:02:09.394
All based on real technologies

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:12.160
that humans are using
in some form already.

00:02:12.327 --> 00:02:14.027
Let's see how they work.

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:16.194
[The Star Laser]

00:02:16.394 --> 00:02:18.860
As an advanced technological civilization,

00:02:18.927 --> 00:02:21.294
the Smorpians harness
the energy of their star

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:24.560
by surrounding it with billions
of solar power satellites.

00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:28.860
This Dyson swarm collects 1%
of the star's energy output,

00:02:28.927 --> 00:02:31.660
a million billion billion watts,

00:02:31.727 --> 00:02:35.027
50 billion times more
than all humanity generates.

00:02:35.527 --> 00:02:37.727
What if all the power
of the Dyson swarm,

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:41.160
all those satellites were used
to create a star laser?

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:45.094
Like any laser, the bigger it is,
the longer its range.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:48.160
Human-built lasers
use small mirrors to focus,

00:02:48.227 --> 00:02:49.927
so they have short ranges.

00:02:50.227 --> 00:02:53.160
The Smorpians could turn
their entire Dyson swarm

00:02:53.227 --> 00:02:56.927
into a collective focusing element
a million kilometers wide.

00:02:57.460 --> 00:03:00.394
The star laser has an insane
range as a result,

00:03:00.527 --> 00:03:02.527
enough to focus on target Earth

00:03:02.594 --> 00:03:05.294
from a distance of over
2 million light years.

00:03:05.794 --> 00:03:07.794
OK, let's shoot it.

00:03:08.727 --> 00:03:12.327
Countless tiny beams combine
into a single huge beam.

00:03:12.527 --> 00:03:14.760
Laser beams are normally
invisible in space,

00:03:14.827 --> 00:03:16.894
but the star laser is so powerful

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:19.894
that light scattering off bits
of dust and gas in its path

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:21.960
makes it clearly visible in the sky.

00:03:22.227 --> 00:03:24.327
A gigantic column of green light.

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:26.694
The laser travels at the speed of light,

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:29.694
which, oddly enough,
is still pretty slow on a galactic level.

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:33.260
It takes a whole day until the laser
has left the Smorpian system,

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:35.860
shooting into the emptiness between stars.

00:03:36.027 --> 00:03:37.794
It will travel for decades,

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:41.460
occasionally melting the odd bit
of interstellar dust or asteroid.

00:03:42.227 --> 00:03:46.194
42 years after being fired,
it arrives without warning.

00:03:46.427 --> 00:03:49.260
Humans only notice
a weird green glow in the sky,

00:03:49.327 --> 00:03:51.194
and then they're gone.

00:03:51.494 --> 00:03:53.394
1% of the energy of a star,

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:55.960
concentrated into a beam
the diameter of Earth,

00:03:56.027 --> 00:03:58.160
traveling 42 light years.

00:03:58.227 --> 00:04:00.360
It burns the exposed half of the planet

00:04:00.427 --> 00:04:02.894
with the intensity of 3 million Suns.

00:04:03.127 --> 00:04:06.327
The seas boil and evaporate,
fires scour the land,

00:04:06.394 --> 00:04:10.160
and within minutes Earth's crust
begins to melt into a sea of lava.

00:04:10.227 --> 00:04:11.560
As the planet rotates,

00:04:11.627 --> 00:04:15.127
it turns into a red hot hell
with no trace of life.

00:04:15.427 --> 00:04:18.327
After a day, it's all over
and the laser dies down.

00:04:18.427 --> 00:04:19.927
In another 42 years,

00:04:19.994 --> 00:04:22.594
the Smorpians will know
if they've been successful.

00:04:22.694 --> 00:04:24.760
That's another thing
about interstellar war.

00:04:24.827 --> 00:04:28.627
When you attack, your grandchildren
will be the ones to find out if you won.

00:04:29.294 --> 00:04:32.594
It's like all the bombs from World War II
exploding in the 80s

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:35.260
and us only seeing the effect today.

00:04:35.694 --> 00:04:39.794
OK, the star laser's extreme range,
speed of light attack,

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:41.960
and ability to melt down any target

00:04:42.027 --> 00:04:44.527
make it a premier interstellar weapon.

00:04:44.627 --> 00:04:46.327
But is there something else?

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:49.260
[The Relativistic Missile]

00:04:49.727 --> 00:04:54.027
What if instead of converting the energy
of their Dyson swarm into a laser,

00:04:54.094 --> 00:04:57.094
the Smorpians used it
to shoot a super bullet?

00:04:57.260 --> 00:05:01.360
A relativistic missile going as close
to the speed of light as possible.

00:05:01.827 --> 00:05:03.727
This sort of weapon is at the limits

00:05:03.794 --> 00:05:05.927
of what the Smorpian
technology can handle,

00:05:05.994 --> 00:05:09.994
as it requires loads of a highly
dangerous material: antimatter.

00:05:10.127 --> 00:05:12.327
The evil twin of regular matter.

00:05:12.694 --> 00:05:16.094
Humans have only managed to produce
a few nanograms of antimatter.

00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:18.060
With their unlimited energy,

00:05:18.127 --> 00:05:21.094
Smorpians can manufacture it
at an industrial scale

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:23.060
to build antimatter rockets.

00:05:23.294 --> 00:05:26.227
When antimatter and matter are mixed,
they annihilate,

00:05:26.294 --> 00:05:29.627
which in more practical terms
means there's a big big boom

00:05:29.694 --> 00:05:31.794
releasing gamma rays and plasma.

00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:33.760
The physics is complicated,

00:05:33.827 --> 00:05:37.094
but basically, if you have
a really strong magnetic field

00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:39.327
you can deflect the plasma
through a nozzle

00:05:39.394 --> 00:05:41.794
just like in the chemical rockets
humans use.

00:05:41.894 --> 00:05:44.294
But it would be much, much faster.

00:05:44.427 --> 00:05:47.027
The fastest rocket possibly basically.

00:05:47.194 --> 00:05:50.794
Our relativistic missile
is much bigger than a skyscraper.

00:05:51.327 --> 00:05:55.327
At the bottom is the bell shaped
magnetic nozzle 100 meters wide.

00:05:55.827 --> 00:05:59.927
On top of it are 250 floors
filled with antimatter and matter

00:05:59.994 --> 00:06:01.694
ready to annihilate each other.

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:04.394
On the top floor
is a 300 kilogram projectile

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:07.027
looking quite small,
about the size of a person.

00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:09.660
To stop them getting damaged on the way,

00:06:09.727 --> 00:06:12.027
the missiles have dozens
of sacrificial layers

00:06:12.094 --> 00:06:13.594
that form a Whipple Shield.

00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:15.460
To make sure they do their job,

00:06:15.527 --> 00:06:18.127
the Smorpians build 1000 missiles.

00:06:18.827 --> 00:06:20.327
Let's fire them.

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:23.960
Launching all the relativistic missiles
is a spectacular event.

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:28.460
For a moment, the antimatter engines
lighting up outshine their star.

00:06:29.194 --> 00:06:31.794
Their exhaust is a long trail
of brilliant white,

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:33.427
and as they accelerate away,

00:06:33.494 --> 00:06:36.794
they appear redder and redder
until they turn invisible.

00:06:36.994 --> 00:06:40.660
With the extreme amount of energy released
by the matter-antimatter reactions,

00:06:40.727 --> 00:06:42.394
the missiles are accelerated

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:47.460
to 99.9999996%
of the speed of light.

00:06:47.927 --> 00:06:50.127
They have effectively infinite range,

00:06:50.194 --> 00:06:52.460
as there's nothing really
to slow them down.

00:06:52.794 --> 00:06:55.094
They arrive shortly
after you can see them.

00:06:55.394 --> 00:06:58.627
The light from their launch
will take 42 years to reach Earth,

00:06:58.694 --> 00:07:02.127
so human astronomers might see
the flash of the missile's launch,

00:07:02.194 --> 00:07:04.627
and then a few days later they'll hit.

00:07:04.694 --> 00:07:06.494
Not enough time to prepare.

00:07:06.994 --> 00:07:09.727
Each relativistic missile
packs the kinetic energy

00:07:09.794 --> 00:07:11.494
of a dinosaur killer asteroid,

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:13.360
so only one needs to hit.

00:07:13.727 --> 00:07:15.194
They never reach the ground,

00:07:15.260 --> 00:07:18.160
disintegrating instead
at the edge of Earth's atmosphere.

00:07:18.627 --> 00:07:21.794
Intense blue flashes
set everything on fire.

00:07:22.060 --> 00:07:25.594
Then continent-sized fireballs
slam down on the surface

00:07:25.694 --> 00:07:28.694
to smash everything into dust, repeatedly,

00:07:28.827 --> 00:07:31.694
until nothing is left
but rubble and smoke.

00:07:32.027 --> 00:07:35.094
So interstellar missiles
with unlimited range,

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:39.360
minimal warning, and delivering complete
destruction of a planet's surface.

00:07:39.694 --> 00:07:40.794
Nice.

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:43.060
But they are a hassle to build.

00:07:43.527 --> 00:07:45.294
Is there something else maybe?

00:07:46.027 --> 00:07:48.794
[The Ultra-Relativistic Electron Beam]

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:51.060
Humans do funny things to their food

00:07:51.127 --> 00:07:53.660
to rid it of bacteria
and make it safe to eat,

00:07:53.727 --> 00:07:55.927
like shooting electron beams
at strawberries.

00:07:56.227 --> 00:07:59.127
Small particle accelerators
send electrons into the food

00:07:59.227 --> 00:08:02.427
with an energy similar to the radiation
from nuclear reactions.

00:08:03.094 --> 00:08:05.994
Not enough to burn the food,
but deadly to bacteria.

00:08:06.627 --> 00:08:09.327
Smorpians had the same idea,
but bigger.

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:12.660
The main challenge
with an electron beam is range.

00:08:12.827 --> 00:08:15.127
Electrons are negatively
charged particles,

00:08:15.194 --> 00:08:17.194
so they don't want to stay
near each other.

00:08:17.494 --> 00:08:19.794
A regular electron beam
will quickly spread out,

00:08:19.860 --> 00:08:21.260
making it harmless.

00:08:21.427 --> 00:08:24.660
Smorpians needed to cover distances
of dozens of light years,

00:08:24.727 --> 00:08:28.127
so they've used the rules
of the universe to trick the electrons

00:08:28.227 --> 00:08:32.060
by building an Ultra-Relativistic
Electron Beam, or UREB.

00:08:32.127 --> 00:08:34.360
What it does is accelerate the electrons

00:08:34.460 --> 00:08:37.827
to 99.99999…

00:08:37.894 --> 00:08:39.894
…99999…

00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:42.127
…99999…

00:08:42.194 --> 00:08:43.994
…99999…

00:08:44.060 --> 00:08:48.027
…9999998% of the speed of light.

00:08:48.094 --> 00:08:49.094
Phew!

00:08:49.160 --> 00:08:52.160
Faster than even
the most powerful cosmic rays.

00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:54.960
The closer something travels
to the speed of light,

00:08:55.027 --> 00:08:58.627
the slower time moves for it
relative to the rest of the universe.

00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:02.127
And since these electrons
are moving so incredibly fast,

00:09:02.194 --> 00:09:04.394
for every second of spreading
their experience,

00:09:04.460 --> 00:09:07.360
over 5 million years pass in real time.

00:09:07.827 --> 00:09:11.227
A physics trick that lets the beam
cross interstellar distances

00:09:11.294 --> 00:09:13.794
while remaining
tightly focused on its target.

00:09:14.194 --> 00:09:17.994
The biggest particle accelerator on Earth
is 27 kilometers long.

00:09:18.760 --> 00:09:22.460
The Smorpians need one
that's over 100,000 kilometers long.

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:25.860
A megastructure 8 times longer
than Earth is wide.

00:09:26.227 --> 00:09:30.127
It's mostly a tube of magnets holding
the beam together until the exit.

00:09:30.594 --> 00:09:34.794
Like a long trumpet of doom
surrounded by an aura of deadly radiation.

00:09:35.127 --> 00:09:39.827
When it's fired, it produces a ruler
straight lightning bolt pointed at Earth.

00:09:40.127 --> 00:09:43.427
Its effects on arrival are less visible
than the other weapons.

00:09:43.727 --> 00:09:46.460
No flashes of light,
no massive firestorms,

00:09:46.527 --> 00:09:48.027
no explosions.

00:09:48.360 --> 00:09:51.160
It doesn't destroy rocks,
it destroys DNA.

00:09:51.527 --> 00:09:55.527
People get dizzy, then fall sick
as their cells are pierced by radiation.

00:09:55.994 --> 00:09:59.694
You might think that a deep bunker
could save a few humans, but no.

00:09:59.894 --> 00:10:01.627
The UREB is so penetrating

00:10:01.694 --> 00:10:05.027
that its effects accumulate
to lethal doses even underground,

00:10:05.094 --> 00:10:06.694
over days or weeks.

00:10:06.760 --> 00:10:09.194
In the end, just like our strawberries,

00:10:09.294 --> 00:10:11.394
Earth becomes sterile.

00:10:12.594 --> 00:10:14.494
[Simulation results]

00:10:14.660 --> 00:10:18.760
Hm, another elaborate animated
science explainer by Kurzgesagt

00:10:18.827 --> 00:10:21.227
where we've learned a lot,
not sure exactly what.

00:10:21.960 --> 00:10:25.160
Luckily, the Smorpians don't really exist,

00:10:25.227 --> 00:10:27.027
but others… might.

00:10:27.294 --> 00:10:29.394
One major downside of all our weapons

00:10:29.460 --> 00:10:32.427
is that others around the Milky Way
could see you firing them,

00:10:32.494 --> 00:10:33.527
which is not ideal

00:10:33.594 --> 00:10:36.294
because you don't want to present
yourself as a dangerous species

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:38.394
and tell everybody where exactly you are.

00:10:38.694 --> 00:10:42.094
So maybe instead of shouting
or shooting out into the universe,

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:45.560
the best course of action seems to be
to stay relatively quiet for now,

00:10:45.627 --> 00:10:47.027
and observe.

00:10:47.394 --> 00:10:50.960
Maybe one day we'll witness
distant stars shooting at each other

00:10:51.027 --> 00:10:53.427
and be glad we stayed out of it.

00:10:54.627 --> 00:10:57.627
But we don't have to stay out
of intergalactic fun.

00:10:57.760 --> 00:11:00.394
There's a peaceful way
to join Type II civilizations

00:11:00.460 --> 00:11:02.260
on their galactic adventures.

00:11:02.460 --> 00:11:04.560
Look! It's the Galactic Club!

00:11:04.694 --> 00:11:06.627
A cozy corner in the vast universe

00:11:06.694 --> 00:11:09.427
reserved for friendly,
quirky folk like you.

00:11:09.794 --> 00:11:11.327
Come in and don't worry,

00:11:11.394 --> 00:11:13.560
we've got everything you need
to fit right in.

00:11:13.627 --> 00:11:15.727
It's all part of our latest limited drop.

00:11:16.294 --> 00:11:18.927
Kill your alien friends with kindness

00:11:18.994 --> 00:11:22.160
and impress them with these
colourful patches and sweaters.

00:11:22.427 --> 00:11:26.660
Wear these new iconic T-shirts
that represent your love of stargazing.

00:11:26.894 --> 00:11:29.060
and show allegiance to our…

00:11:29.127 --> 00:11:31.127
(modified voice)
Ultimate Overlord Duck.

00:11:31.360 --> 00:11:32.960
And the star of the show:

00:11:33.027 --> 00:11:34.394
a woven space blanket

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:37.227
to wrap yourself
and your new alien buddies in.

00:11:37.394 --> 00:11:39.894
Maybe the coolest thing
we've ever created.

00:11:39.960 --> 00:11:41.560
Definitely the largest.

00:11:41.660 --> 00:11:43.394
Like with our last limited drop,

00:11:43.460 --> 00:11:46.327
these items are available now
until they sell out,

00:11:46.394 --> 00:11:48.027
and then never again.

00:11:48.294 --> 00:11:51.694
Pair them up with the 12,024
Cosmic Creations calendar

00:11:51.760 --> 00:11:55.294
to have a beautiful daily reminder
of potential alien civilizations

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:58.160
and a way to make plans
with all your new pals.

00:11:58.227 --> 00:12:00.394
All of our products are designed
and produced with love and care

00:12:00.460 --> 00:12:01.994
by us here at Kurzgesagt.

00:12:02.260 --> 00:12:05.594
They are an integral part
of the science story we try to tell.

00:12:05.694 --> 00:12:07.760
So start your journey on our channel

00:12:07.827 --> 00:12:11.227
and continue it with our posters,
calendars and plushies.

00:12:11.394 --> 00:12:14.394
Every purchase directly funds
what we do on this channel.

00:12:14.527 --> 00:12:16.494
Thank you so much for your support!

00:12:16.894 --> 00:12:18.694
Join the Galactic Club now!

00:12:19.127 --> 00:12:20.527
Overlord Duck…

00:12:20.594 --> 00:12:22.194
(modified voice)
is waiting.

